   Source: https://github.com/facebook/akd

   This repository began as a copy of the `akd` and `akd_core` crates and
   retains their public wire types (`AkdLabel`, `AkdValue`, `LookupProof`,
   `EpochHash`, the storage and VRF layers, and the protobuf definitions
   for those) so that downstream callers can migrate without rewrites.

   Modifications made by The Aegon Authors:

     * The SEEMless/Merkle append-only-tree backend is no longer the engine
       behind `Directory`. Publish, lookup, and consistency now route through
       the Aegon engine (`akd::aegon`), which is built on KZH-k polynomial
       commitments and sharded across N hosts coordinated over gRPC.
     * `Directory` methods tied to the Merkle/VRF version model
       (`key_history`, `audit`, `poll_for_azks_changes`) are retained in the
       API surface but are not implemented against the Aegon backend; the
       Aegon-native equivalents live in `akd::aegon_facade`.
     * New subsystems with no upstream counterpart: the sharded coordinator
       and shard servers, distributed SRS generation, the masking-server
       pool, the Sigma-protocol blinding-equality proof, and IVC
       (fast-forward) auditing under the `ivc_audit` feature.
     * The upstream test suite for the append-only tree
       (`akd::append_only_zks`, `akd::tests`) is retained but is not
       exercised by the Aegon backend. See README for current status.

   Files derived from upstream carry the original Meta copyright header.
   Files authored for Aegon carry a header naming The Aegon Authors.

